## 5. Prioritized Recommendations

### 🔴 Priority 1 — Critical (Core Workflow Gaps)
These are the features that prevent the system from being used for its primary purpose:

1. **MLEF Data Entry Page** — Create a full form to edit `mlef_records` (injury details, consent, wound types, category of hurt, alcohol status)
2. **Clinical Case Detail View** — A page showing all data for a single case (patient info, MLEF, observations, investigations, referrals, report status)
3. **Autopsy Case Detail View** — Same as above for autopsy (cadaver info, PMR, death certificate, voice dictations)
4. **Cause of Death Form Page** — A form to fill in `death_certificates` (immediate/antecedent/contributory causes)
5. **Wound Chart Entry** — A form for `wound_charts` (wound type, weapon, anatomical location)

### 🟡 Priority 2 — Important (Document Management)
6. **Investigation Request Management** — Create/track test requests (X-ray, blood, toxicology, swabs) and view results
7. **Consultation Referral Management** — Create and track specialist referrals
8. **Photograph Upload & Gallery** — Upload and view case photographs
9. **MLR/PMR Status Tracking Pages** — View and update report statuses through their lifecycle
10. **Per-Doctor "My Cases" Filter** — Filter all views by assigned doctor

### 🟢 Priority 3 — Nice-to-Have (Advanced Features)
11. **Auto-Generate Reports** — Template-based MLR/PMR generation
12. **MLEF & PM Registers** — Searchable register views
13. **Case Type Classification** — Add fields for clinical case categories
14. **Death Type Classification** — Add manner-of-death field for autopsy
15. **Digital Histology Repository** — Specialized histology image storage
16. **Voice Dictation Recording** — Audio upload and transcript management

