## Architecture Assessment

| Aspect | Rating | Notes |
|--------|:------:|-------|
| Database Schema | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Excellent. 28 tables cover nearly all requirements |
| Stored Procedures | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Good. 6 procedures handle key transactions |
| Triggers | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Excellent. Temporal validation, chain of custody, audit trails, immutability |
| Backend Routes | ⭐⭐ | Weak. Only 5 route files covering basic CRUD |
| Frontend Templates | ⭐⭐ | Weak. Only registration forms and list views; no detail/edit pages |
| Role-Based Access | ⭐⭐⭐ | Adequate. Roles exist but granular permissions not enforced |
| Notification System | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Good. Working alerts with dismiss functionality |
| Report Generation | ⭐ | Almost non-existent. Only basic daily/pending list views |

> [!TIP]
> **The good news**: Your database layer is production-quality. The 28-table schema, 6 stored procedures, and 8 triggers provide a very solid foundation. The majority of the work needed is building **UI pages and routes** that expose the data already structured in the database. This is significantly easier than redesigning the schema.
